{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795625157,"nonce":"pv8SlCsB9BAhBDGmlMaVR2PWa1g=","title":"A node mounted late with a reactive attribute or class loses align-items, justify-content and six more layout rules","message":"`apply_element_style_to_taffy` (renderer/stylesheet/apply.rs) folds a stylesheet rule into a node's snapshot style and into its class and state layers, and it applied none of `flex-direction`, `flex-wrap`, `align-items`, `justify-content`, `align-self` or `overflow`, `overflow-x`, `overflow-y`, while the layout pass applies them all.\n\nA node with `attr_when` or `class_when` that mounts after the first frame takes the class layer (a snapshot made before the layout pass) first, so `refold_node` writes its style from a snapshot that never got those rules. A `.cn-toggle` inside `show` lost `.blinc-toggle`'s centring: its icon sat at the top. A state or reactive class rule that sets any of the eight also did nothing.\n\nReproducer: a `show` that builds a `div` with `attr_when` and a rule giving it `align-items: center; justify-content: flex-end`.","files":null}]}